/// A type implementing `Named` gets `.name`: the qualified name and the generic arity of the concrete type of the object.
/// For ``North: Named{}`` in the package ``hello``, ``North.name`` is `` `hello.North` ``.
/// For ``Box[T]: Named{}`` in the package ``hello``, ``Box[Nat].name`` is `` `hello.Box[_]` ``.
Named: { read .name: Str -> _Magic!; }
